title: JushiD2_Phones

position: 2259,1812

---

(A phone rings.)

Hou: Hello? Hello?

(Hou snatches up her phone.)

Hou: There's no seat for me at dinner?

Hou: How dare you? I gave birth to that child!

Hou: What do you mean, you paid for all four years of his undergraduate education?

Hou: I may not have paid his tuition, but he is my flesh and blood. I put everything I had into raising him, too.

Hou: You old man—

Hou: What do you mean, I didn't take him with me?

Hou: He has his drunkard father's surname, not mine! You wouldn't let me take him. Doesn't he have your name?

Hou: His grandmother would cry just from washing his clothes!

Hou: I...

Hou: I gave in for just one moment, and...

Hou: I had to work.

(Hou scratches her scalp in agitation, lets out a long sigh, and lowers her voice.)

Hou: Tell me something. Who will Chang Yuantao's son call Grandma someday?

Hou: (Her voice rises again.) Chang Yuantao's stepmother?

Hou: Or that great-grandmother of his, who calls her own grandson *aoni*—"son"!

(She suddenly laughs, very gently, ends the call in one swift motion, and dials another number.)

//Pause the dialogue panel here; press Space to show it again.

<<pause_dialogue>>

Hou: Oh! Principal Kuai.

Hou: Yes, Principal Kuai. And how is your wife? Both well, I hope.

Hou: I have a meditation event today, so it's rather difficult for me to get away. Mm-hmm.

Hou: Of course, you're most welcome. Yuantao told me all about it.

Hou: I'm terribly sorry. He came back to China and stayed at your home for two whole weeks. We must have imposed.

Hou: Had he told us, we would never have let him be so discourteous.

Hou: Thank you for being so understanding.

Hou: Yes, yes, of course.

(She grips the phone, cupping half her face and the hand holding it with her other hand, listening gravely.)

(The warmth she had summoned for the call melts away from her face. She bites her lip and nods silently.)

Hou: Yes. Oh, the two of them are doing well together.

(Hou smiles gently, and the warmth surges back into her face.)

Hou: Mm-hmm. I'll have the gift delivered today, though I won't be able to come myself.

Hou: Let's meet again after Yuantao's grandfather and the family have paid a visit to Chongqing.

Hou: Mm. (She touches her burning cheek and ends the call.)

[You hear MBTI and Bilbo calling.]

Hou: (Smiling gently at you.) Haha. No need to rush now.

Hou: You heard all that. I won't pretend otherwise.

Hou: Have a local courier take the gift to the Kempinski.

Hou: Mm. That'll do.

Hou: Wrap it nicely. Take your time. No rush anymore.

Hou: I want it to arrive around six, when they're halfway through dinner.

Hou: As for what to give them... we can take our time choosing.

Hou: What were those collections you mentioned earlier?

(You gently turn the catalog back to the contents page.)

//Pause the dialogue panel here; press Space to show it again.

<<pause_dialogue>>

<<if ($D2TriedFamily or $D2TriedWelcome) and ($D2TriedSmall or $D2TriedBird or $D2TriedPeach)>>

