title: JushiD2_HeHuan

position: 384,237

---

Hou: Harmony? As in harmony between husband and wife?

Me: That can certainly be one auspicious meaning.

Me: But there's also a local story in Yixing that Chen Mansheng designed it after seeing a pair of large cymbals.

(You turn to page seven of the catalog and lay it open in front of Hou.)

//Pause the dialogue panel here; press Space to show it again.

<<pause_dialogue>>

Hou: (Interrupting.) Cymbals?

Hou: The kind people bang at celebrations?

Hou: (She smiles gently.) What does that have to do with tonight?

-> Before Chen Mansheng, zisha teapots were largely consumed by scholars and men of letters.

    <<jump JushiD2_HeHuanHistory>>

-> He designed it after a celebration banquet.

