title: JushiD2_DaughterInLawIntro

---

Hou: I'll tell you something. To be frank, I don't like this girl.

Me: Why? Haven't you said you've never met her?

Hou: Hmph. For one thing, they're living together before marriage. (She bites her lip again.)

Hou: My son only comes back once a year. This time he didn't even come back to Yixing.

Hou: Without a word, that girl took him off to Chongqing.

Hou: It left us with no say in any of it.

(She clicks her tongue.)

<<jump JushiD2_AfterGiftChoice2>>

===

title: JushiD2_DaughterInLaw

---

// Continue from here.

Hou: You girls put everything online these days, don't you?

Hou: She listens to rock music, with all that black stuff around her eyes and on her lips.

Hou: A while ago she was making a fuss about some menstruation thing. How can she be so shameless?

Hou: And she was campaigning for that pink-haired girl who took her own life. Good heavens.

Hou: You don't understand. You don't understand.

Hou: My son is a very, very kind person.

Hou: He's always looking after other people's feelings, always putting himself last.

Hou: His grandparents brought him up all wrong!

Hou: I'm the sort of person who knows how to resist, too. I could never get along with them.

(Hou bites at the dead skin on her lip.)

Hou: You only live once. You should live as you please, without worrying so much about everyone else.

Me: Well, if she wants to study abroad and listen to rock, maybe she's trying to make her own choices too.

Hou: That's her business.

Hou: Can I control her? I can't even control my own son.

(She glances at her phone.)

Hou: My son can't handle a girl with that much rebellion in her.

Hou: I mean it. She had such a good undergraduate record. She turned down a guaranteed graduate-school place just to see what studying abroad would be like.

Hou: She's got a scholarship, too.

Hou: My son isn't as clever. He only meant to try applying for grad school, maybe look for a job while he was at it.

Hou: She pushed him into it.

Hou: He can't handle her. He's kind, and if she gets him under her thumb, he'll suffer for it.

Hou: I never encouraged him to date at this age. It's all because his grandfather kept pushing him.

[You hear Bilbo calling.]

<<jump JushiD2_PackRemaining>>

