title: JushiD2_Delivery

position: 265,2037

---

You quietly finish up what you're doing.

(Hou slowly turns toward the window.

The sun is beginning to set. There are fewer people on Gunan Street now.

Some push their bicycles; others start their electric scooters with a couple of little chirps.

Here and there, a beetle-like car pulls away.

Your gaze moves from the backlit window frame to her.

She is thin, with very short hair, alert and spirited.

The skin on her face clings tightly to her bones, yet her cheeks are not hollow.

Dim orange sunlight catches her cheekbones, neck, and pronounced wrist bones.

After all that commotion, no one has switched on the shop lights. Beyond the glow around her, everything looks dark and cold.

She seems warmly dressed, though:

a dusty-pink cashmere twinset, its pills carefully trimmed, with slightly worn plastic buttons in the same shade.

She smiles very gently.)

//Pause the dialogue panel here; press Space to show it again.

<<pause_dialogue>>

Me: It's all wrapped. I'll send it over at six.

Hou: Not send it at six. I want it delivered by six.

Hou: About thirty minutes into dinner. Room 1314 at the Kempinski.

Hou: I'll be off. You can record the sale here; I'll transfer the money straight to Shao Wei.

Hou: By the way, what's your name?

Me: My surname is Wang.

Hou: Wang. Thank you for all your trouble.

You watch her walk down the lane. There's nothing else to do today. What will she take to leave Gunan Street?

Her figure turns right at the end of the lane and disappears.

<<hide_character "jushi">>

<<jump JushiD2_Teacher>>

===

title: JushiD2_Teacher

position: 265,2262

---

<<wait 0.4>>

<<play_sfx "doorbell">>

<<wait 0.8>>

<<show_character "teacher">>

<<wait 0.3>>

Shao Wei: (She pushes the door open, speaking on speakerphone.)

(She drops a bag onto the table, gestures toward you with her chin, and covers the receiver.)

Shao Wei: I brought these from Huanglong Mountain for you this week. Everything all right?

(Before you can answer, she goes back to the phone.)

Shao Wei: Oh, sis! What brings you here today?

Shao Wei: All good, all good. Mm-hmm.

Shao Wei: This girl here? She's very capable, you know.

Shao Wei: In a hurry to get home? Well, take care! Yes, yes. Bye now.

Shao Wei: (She hangs up and turns to you.)

//Pause the dialogue panel here; press Space to show it again.

<<pause_dialogue>>

(It's the same tall, impeccably dressed Shao Wei.)

//Pause the dialogue panel here; press Space to show it again.

<<pause_dialogue>>

Shao Wei: What do you know about her?

Shao Wei: Oh, her life used to be so comfortable.

Shao Wei: Her father-in-law was somebody in the county government. (She gives a thumbs-up.) Back when they were courting investment, they were riding high!

Shao Wei: She married into quite the family. Lived very well.

Shao Wei: Her sister-in-law was even her best friend from high school. The whole family doted on her little boy.

Shao Wei: She wasn't like this back then. Looked down her nose at everyone, always boasting about her husband's family.

Shao Wei: She and her husband had easy jobs, kept their salaries for themselves, and lived and ate at home. Oh, the things they spent money on!

Shao Wei: Then someone reported her. Such a petty little person. Ruined her chances of promotion.

Shao Wei: They found problems in the accounts at her father's company, too.

Shao Wei: Ah, if they'd only held on a few more years, the whole company might have been theirs. Why the hurry?

[At the same moment that you call out to Ke Xiang, you hear Ke Xiang calling to you.]

Shao Wei: Such is fate!

Shao Wei: Even her father-in-law was investigated.

Shao Wei: Nothing came of it in the end, but how could they go on living under the same roof?

Shao Wei: And right at that moment, her husband moved out. Only later did they find out...

Me: He ran off with the money?

Shao Wei: That drunken fool!

Shao Wei: Him? As if he could pull that off! He had another woman!

Shao Wei: That man had been spoiled rotten since childhood. He kicked up a fuss until he got his divorce and married someone else.

Shao Wei: Her own family couldn't help her. Miserable, really.

Shao Wei: In the first lunar month of 2008,

Shao Wei: she finally moved out for good. She deliberately waited until her son had fallen asleep.

Shao Wei: They loaded the last box of her personal things into the car.

Shao Wei: The engine started, the headlights came on,

Shao Wei: and there was the little boy, standing at the courtyard gate.

Shao Wei: Crying in his grandmother's arms, calling out for his mother.

Shao Wei: His grandmother couldn't possibly let him go running after her. His father would've beaten him for it!

Shao Wei: Both of them crying. Mother and son.

Shao Wei: Oh, I've heard her tell that story more times than I can count.

Shao Wei: The house, the son—what could she take with her?

Shao Wei: And you haven't seen that new wife of his!

Shao Wei: She used to work under Hou Li. Who knows how often Hou looked down her nose at her.

Shao Wei: (Tsk.) What a miserable business.

-> Aren't you her friend?

    <<jump JushiD2_TeacherFriend>>

-> Couldn't she have refused to divorce him?

    <<jump JushiD2_TeacherDivorce>>

===

title: JushiD2_TeacherFriend

position: 512,2487

---

Shao Wei: Of course. Why would I ask you to look after her if we weren't friends?

Me: ...Oh... nothing.

Shao Wei: Huh? What did I say that was so bad about her?

Shao Wei: (She glances down at her phone.)

Shao Wei: Yixing is only so big. Everyone knows everybody's family business.

Shao Wei: It's hardly a secret.

<<jump JushiD2_Order>>

===

title: JushiD2_TeacherDivorce

position: 232,2487

---

Shao Wei: (She pauses.)

Shao Wei: Ah. What happens between husband and wife is never something you can explain in a sentence or two.

Shao Wei: Marriage, eh!

Shao Wei: She's been through enough over the years.

Shao Wei: A woman starting over doesn't need every old story dragged out again.

Me: ...

Shao Wei: Look, she practices meditation, does good deeds, and leads a quiet life now.

Shao Wei: What's wrong with that?

<<jump JushiD2_Order>>

